  "introduction": "SUPPLICATIONS AFTER THE ZIYARAH\n\nSayyid Ibn Tawus has stated that it is recommended to say the following supplicatory prayer immediately after performing the rites of visitation to the Holy Imams (‘a):\n\nYou may now kiss the holy tomb, put your two cheeks on it, and say the following words:\n\nYou may now offer the prayer of ziyarah. If you intend to bid farewell to the visited holy person and leave, you may say the following words:\n\nShaykh al-Mufid has also mentioned these words, but he added: After the statement, you may say the following words:\n\nA visitor of any of the holy shrines, or any suppliant wherever he may be and whatever prayer he may say, is highly recommended to begin with praying Almighty Allah for the good of Imam al-Mahdi, Almighty Allah’s argument in this age and the patron of the divine mission. Although this issue is of great importance and brings about many significant advantages, it seems unsuitable to refer to this importance or mention these advantages in this place.\n\nHowever, Shaykh al-Nuri, in Chapter Ten of his book of al-Najm al-Thaqib, has discussed this issue in details and mentioned some supplications in this regard. It is thus recommended to refer to this chapter. The briefest supplication in this connection has been previously cited in this book within the recommended acts at the twenty-third night of Ramazan. It is the following supplication:\n\nWithin the etiquettes of visiting Imam al-Husayn (‘a), I have mentioned another supplication that can be said at all of the holy shrines. The supplication begins with the following statement:",
  "versesCount": 77,
  "verses": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "arabic": "اَللّٰهُمَّ اِنْ كَانَتْ ذُنُوْبِيْ",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "arabic": "قَدْ اَخْلَقَتْ وَجْهِيْ عِنْدَكَ",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "arabic": "وَ حَجَبَتْ دُعَاۤئِيْ عَنْكَ",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "arabic": "وَ حَالَتْ بَيْنِيْ وَ بَيْنَكَ",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "arabic": "فَاَسْاَلُكَ اَنْ تُقْبِلَ عَلَيَّ بِوَجْهِكَ الْكَرِيْمِ",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "arabic": "وَ تَنْشُرَ عَلَيَّ رَحْمَتَكَ",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "arabic": "وَ تُنَزِّلَ عَلَيَّ بَرَكَاتِكَ",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "arabic": "وَ اِنْ كَانَتْ قَدْ مَنَعَتْ اَنْ تَرْفَعَ لِيۤ اِلَيْكَ صَوْتًا",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "arabic": "اَوْ تَغْفِرَ لِيْ ذَنْبًا",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "arabic": "اَوْ تَتَجَاوَزَ عَنْ خَطِيْئَةٍ مُهْلِكَةٍ",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "arabic": "فَهَاۤ اَنَا ذَا مُسْتَجِيْرٌ بِكَرَمِ وَجْهِكَ",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "arabic": "وَ عِزِّ جَلَالِكَ",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "arabic": "مُتَوَسِّلٌ اِلَيْكَ مُتَقَرِّبٌ اِلَيْكَ",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "arabic": "بِاَحَبِّ خَلْقِكَ اِلَيْكَ",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "arabic": "وَ اَكْرَمِهِمْ عَلَيْكَ",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "arabic": "وَ اَوْلَاهُمْ بِكَ",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "arabic": "وَ اَطْوَعِهِمْ لَكَ",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "arabic": "وَ اَعْظَمِهِمْ مَنْزِلَةً وَ مَكَانًا عِنْدَكَ",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "arabic": "مُحَمَّدٍ وَ بِعِتْرَتِهِ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "arabic": "الْاَئِمَّةِ الْهُدَاةِ الْمَهْدِيِّيْنَ",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "arabic": "الَّذِيْنَ فَرَضْتَ عَلٰى خَلْقِكَ طَاعَتَهُمْ",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "arabic": "وَ اَمَرْتَ بِمَوَدَّتِهِمْ",
